Source: rustc
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Docker Hardened Images <dhi@docker.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://www.rust-lang.org/

Package: rustc
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, binutils, gcc, libc6-dev
Conflicts: rustup, rustc-1.96, rustc-1.97, rustc-1.98, rustc-1.99, rustc-1.100
Replaces: rustc-1.96, rustc-1.97, rustc-1.98, rustc-1.99, rustc-1.100
Description: Rust systems programming language
 Rust is a curly-brace, block-structured expression language. It visually
 resembles the C language family, but differs significantly in syntactic and
 semantic details. This package provides the Rust compiler, rustdoc, and the
 standard library.

Package: cargo
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, rustc (= ${binary:Version}), binutils, gcc
Conflicts: rustup, cargo-1.96, cargo-1.97, cargo-1.98, cargo-1.99, cargo-1.100
Replaces: cargo-1.96, cargo-1.97, cargo-1.98, cargo-1.99, cargo-1.100
Description: Rust package manager
 Cargo is a tool that allows Rust projects to declare their various
 dependencies and ensure repeatable builds. This package provides Cargo for
 the Rust toolchain shipped by the rustc package of the same version.

Package: rustfmt
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, rustc (= ${binary:Version}), cargo (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: rustup
Description: Rust code formatter
 rustfmt and cargo-fmt format Rust code according to style guidelines. This
 package provides the formatter built from the same source as the rustc
 package of the same version.

Package: rust-clippy
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, rustc (= ${binary:Version}), cargo (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: rustup
Description: Rust linter
 Clippy is a collection of lints to catch common mistakes and improve Rust
 code. This package provides clippy-driver and cargo-clippy built from the
 same source as the rustc package of the same version.
